  "variation": {
    "seeded": true,
    "notes": "Flame licks, ember paths and smoke puffs change per seed; the timing of the three phases does not."
  },
  "director_notes": "A natural, cozy fire for a survival/camping skill, not a spell: no magic colors, no big burst. Ignite is a gentle 1.2 s ease-out so lighting feels earned. The burn beat loops seamlessly between 2.0 s and 6.9 s, which is what a game holds for as long as the fire has fuel; the embers beat is played once when it runs out (the coals glow and the smoke thins, flames gone). Hero view is three-quarter because players see campfires from a third-person camera. Smoke is kept thin and low-opacity so it never hides players sitting by the fire. Built for Sparkfall's Camping skill (Unity, URP): the flames layer's side-view burn frames are the flame flipbook; embers, smoke, glow and light are rebuilt as particle systems and a point light."
